orical) during the 19th century era.","dna16":"8800585866000529","ex":["It reminds me of the advice that Mr. Secretary Corwin gave to a young man that was applying for a clerkship. He said, ‘Young man, go West’.","Go West, young man! Buy a good, stout farming outfit... and then go out to the far West upon Government-land."],"id":"wikt:go west:verb:5","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,81:1","syn":[],"tags":["US"]}]},"go whistle":{"dna16":"8800585867000015","senses":[{"def":"To go to the devil (as a term of dismissal).","dna16":"8800585867000122","ex":["If you're not willing to put in a little effort to help around here, you can go whistle!"],"id":"wikt:go whistle:verb:1","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["derogatory","figuratively","slang"]}]},"go whole hog":{"dna16":"8800585868000014","forms_of":["go the whole hog"],"senses":[]},"go wide":{"dna16":"8800585869000013","senses":[{"def":"To use a wide-angle lens to take one or more photographs.","dna16":"8800585869000120","ex":["1998, Sport Diver. Vol. 6, No. 6. Pg. 36.\nFirst and foremost, you'll need a wide-angle lens for going wide on your dive.","2004. Digital Photography Bible. Dan Simon. Pg. 48.\nYou need to go wide just to fit things in."],"id":"wikt:go wide:verb:1","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"To change frequently.","dna16":"8800585869000229","ex":["The change between futures and spot prices will either go wide -- expand or diminish -- go narrow"],"id":"wikt:go wide:verb:2","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"18:1","syn":[]},{"def":"To spread one's attention from a narrow focus to a more diverse one.","dna16":"8800585869000328","ex":[],"id":"wikt:go wide:verb:3","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]}]},"go wild":{"dna16":"8800585870000010","senses":[{"def":"To become very noisy and excited.","dna16":"8800585870000127","ex":["Brazil scored, and the crowd went wild!"],"id":"wikt:go wild:verb:1","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"96:1","syn":[],"tags":["idiomatic"]},{"d